# Vulnerability details

## Impact
In the `RestakeManager::deposit`function the contract checks the buffer deficit for the withdrawal queue first. Then it
uses the deposited assets to cover the deficit as much as possible by filling the buffer, and if there are any token left
it invests them. The problem is that if there are no tokens left it will revert since it will try to deposit zero.

That means that if there's a buffer deficit the next transaction needs to deposit enough funds to fill it fully in one single
transaction, otherwise it will revert. Partial filling of the buffer is not allowed since there are no funds left and it reverts.
Depending on the needed amount the deposited could be out of service for a long time till someone deposits enough funds.

## Proof of Concept
