    if (price <= 0) revert InvalidOraclePrice();

    // Price is times 10**18 ensure value amount is scaled
    return (uint256(price) * _balance) / SCALE_FACTOR;
}
```

The oracle should account for this fact by using the correct heartbeat for each feed, otherwise the staleness check is not complete and there's a risk of the integrators consuming a stale price.

The heartbeats can be found here:
https://docs.chain.link/data-feeds/price-feeds/addresses/?network=ethereum&page=1
(check `Show more details`)

## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Use a different heartbeat for each feed in accordance to the values provided from Chainlink.



