# Vulnerability details

## Impact
When the protocol issues allocation basis point to different operator delegators, there is a lack of check that the total allocated basis point for all operator delegators involved is not > 10000/100%. This lack of verification will allow the same piece of the Total TVL to be allocated to the different Operator Delegators among other impacts like 

- Process of Distribution of the total TVL will be impended, as some Operator Delegators, will have their share of the total TVL allocated to another Operator Delegator.
- Incorrect TVL Threshold Calculation
- An Operator Delegator that should not be Considered as below the threshold will be incorrectly assumed to be below the threshold.

## Proof of Concept
The issue here is fairly simple to decipher, in a normal calculations, where tokens or deposits are sent to contract and the amount of tokens that each contract will receive is based upon basis points/% the total allocated should not be greater than 10000bps/100%, in any case should this happen then the amount of tokens that will be shared will not be enough for all receiving contract, But in the context of the `RestakeManager` of the Renzo protocol, the impact is more than that as it affects the manner in which Operator Delegators are chosen for deposits and withdrawals.

They are two functions where this check could be enforced but they were not as shown below 

```solidity
 function addOperatorDelegator(
        IOperatorDelegator _newOperatorDelegator,
        uint256 _allocationBasisPoints
    ) external onlyRestakeManagerAdmin {
..more code
        // Verify a valid allocation
        if (_allocationBasisPoints > (100 * BASIS_POINTS)) revert OverMaxBasisPoints();
...more code 
```
In this Function to add new ODs, there is a check to make sure that the current basis point that is about to be allocated is not greater than 100%, but not that the total basis point allocated to each OD is not greater than 100%.

The other function that handles ODs allocation basis point also did not implement this check 

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-renzo/blob/519e518f2d8dec9acf6482b84a181e403070d22d/contracts/RestakeManager.sol#L187C5-L212C6

```solidity
function setOperatorDelegatorAllocation(
        IOperatorDelegator _operatorDelegator,
        uint256 _allocationBasisPoints
    ) external onlyRestakeManagerAdmin {
        if (address(_operatorDelegator) == address(0x0)) revert InvalidZeroInput();
        if (_allocationBasisPoints > (100 * BASIS_POINTS)) revert OverMaxBasisPoints();

        // Ensure the OD is in the list to prevent mis-configuration
        bool foundOd = false;
        uint256 odLength = operatorDelegators.length;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < odLength; ) {
            if (address(operatorDelegators[i]) == address(_operatorDelegator)) {
                foundOd = true;
                break;
            }
            unchecked {
                ++i;
            }
        }
        if (!foundOd) revert NotFound();

        // Set the allocation
        operatorDelegatorAllocations[_operatorDelegator] = _allocationBasisPoints;
}
```
This Also Implements the same Code As the Previous shown example, no check for the total bps that as being allocated, This makes The TotalTVL in the Protocol at any moment unable to meet the ODs required token allocation

We will describe this using 4 Operator delegators with their allocations basis points and the genral total TVL of the protocol

OD1- 3000bps/30%
OD2- 3000bps/30%
OD3- 4000bps/40%
OD4- 3000bps/30%
Total- 13000bps/130%
Total TVL- 10000 

This Means Each ODs has a right to the TVL but the TVL cannot accommodate everyone, and when choosing ODs for deposit this Issue leads to a situation where the function thinks a particular Operator Delegator is under the Threshold, but in reality the TVL has no allocation for It. This situation is described with the affected code below.

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-renzo/blob/519e518f2d8dec9acf6482b84a181e403070d22d/contracts/RestakeManager.sol#L362C5-L389C10

```solidity
function chooseOperatorDelegatorForDeposit(
        uint256[] memory tvls,
        uint256 totalTVL
    ) public view returns (IOperatorDelegator) {
        // Ensure OperatorDelegator list is not empty
        if (operatorDelegators.length == 0) revert NotFound();

        // If there is only one operator delegator, return it
        if (operatorDelegators.length == 1) {
            return operatorDelegators[0];
        }

        // Otherwise, find the operator delegator with TVL below the threshold
        uint256 tvlLength = tvls.length;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < tvlLength; ) {
            if (
                tvls[i] <
                (operatorDelegatorAllocations[operatorDelegators[i]] * totalTVL) /
                    BASIS_POINTS /
                    BASIS_POINTS
            ) {
                return operatorDelegators[i];
            }

            unchecked {
                ++i;
            }
        }
```
In this Function, and With the scenario described before The Last added OD will be incorrectly assumed to be less than the threshold, even though the the TVL does not have enough tokens to Cover the allocations of tokens to it.

## Tools Used
Manual Reveiew

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
A Check should be implemented in the `addOperatorDelegator` and the `setOperatorDelegatorAllocation` to make sure that the total allocations is not more than the maximum which is 10000/100%, this kind of safety check will ensure that the TVL can service all Operator Delegators at any given time based on the allocation bps, and Operator Delegators below threshold are correctly identified and Provided tokens for staking


